---
/* L71 - gold labels: the record of what happened, two labellers, and the floor. */
---

<figure class="fig">
  <div class="fig__frame">
    <img
      class="fig__picture"
      src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}illustrations/L71.jpg`}
      alt="A line drawing of a thick bound ledger lying closed on a workbench, one loose blank card resting on top of it, a second blank card beside it, and a magnifying glass set over the second card."
    />
    <svg
      class="fig__svg"
      viewBox="0 0 640 340"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="L71-fig-title L71-fig-desc"
    >
      <title id="L71-fig-title">Two ways to tag a letter, and what the disagreements cost</title>
      <desc id="L71-fig-desc">
        On the left, two stacked sources of a tag: a system of record that says what
        actually happened, and one person's reading of what should have happened. On
        the right, the same letters tagged independently by two labellers. They agree
        on most cells, shown as a run of filled squares, but differ on the borderline
        ones, shown as a row of open squares in the middle. The disagreement is then
        adjudicated and kept as its own slice. A bar at the bottom shows 95% agreement
        and a 5% floor of inherent error.
      </desc>

      <!-- two sources of a tag -->
      <text x="30" y="34" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" letter-spacing="0.09em" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">TWO SOURCES</text>

      <rect x="30" y="48" width="250" height="58" fill="var(--color-ground)" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="44" y="72" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink)">what actually happened</text>
      <text x="44" y="92" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">read out of the queue</text>

      <rect x="30" y="120" width="250" height="58" fill="var(--color-ground)" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="44" y="144" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">what should have happened</text>
      <text x="44" y="164" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">one person's reading</text>

      <!-- two labellers -->
      <text x="330" y="34" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" letter-spacing="0.09em" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">TWO LABELLERS, INDEPENDENTLY</text>

      <text x="330" y="60" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">A</text>
      <text x="330" y="94" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">B</text>

      <!-- clear-cut: agreement -->
      <g>
        <rect x="352" y="48" width="18" height="18" fill="var(--color-ink)" />
        <rect x="376" y="48" width="18" height="18" fill="var(--color-ink)" />
        <rect x="400" y="48" width="18" height="18" fill="var(--color-ink)" />
        <rect x="424" y="48" width="18" height="18" fill="var(--color-ink)" />
        <rect x="352" y="82" width="18" height="18" fill="var(--color-ink)" />
        <rect x="376" y="82" width="18" height="18" fill="var(--color-ink)" />
        <rect x="400" y="82" width="18" height="18" fill="var(--color-ink)" />
        <rect x="424" y="82" width="18" height="18" fill="var(--color-ink)" />
      </g>
      <text x="452" y="62" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">clear-cut</text>

      <!-- borderline: disagreement -->
      <g>
        <rect x="352" y="116" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" />
        <rect x="376" y="116" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" />
        <rect x="400" y="116" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" />
      </g>
      <g>
        <rect x="352" y="140" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" />
        <rect x="376" y="140" width="18" height="18" fill="var(--color-prussian)" />
        <rect x="400" y="140" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" />
      </g>
      <text x="452" y="132" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">borderline</text>

      <!-- the disagreement travels to adjudication -->
      <path class="m-draw" style="--m-length: 120; --m-duration: 1.1s; --m-delay: 0.3s;" d="M 400 162 C 400 186, 470 182, 486 200" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-prussian)" stroke-width="1" />
      <rect x="486" y="200" width="128" height="46" fill="var(--color-prussian-tint)" stroke="var(--color-prussian)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="500" y="220" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-prussian)">adjudicate</text>
      <text x="500" y="236" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">and keep it</text>

      <!-- the floor -->
      <text x="30" y="230" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" letter-spacing="0.09em" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">THE FLOOR</text>
      <rect x="30" y="240" width="250" height="16" fill="var(--color-ground-deep)" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <rect x="30" y="240" width="238" height="16" fill="var(--color-prussian-tint)" />
      <line x1="268" y1="236" x2="268" y2="260" stroke="var(--color-prussian)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="30" y="274" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">95% agree</text>
      <text x="280" y="274" text-anchor="end" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-prussian)">5%</text>

      <text x="30" y="310" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">a wrong label is not neutral: it rewards the wrong behaviour</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="fig__caption">
    <span class="edge-code">figure L71</span>
    <span class="fig__caption-text">Gold labels come from the record of the work, and the cases two labellers disagree about are the ones that set the floor under every accuracy number.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  /* scoped to this figure */
  .fig__svg {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
</style>
